Dear Mrs. Chen,

I am following up on the case file referred to our office by an FBI IC3
partner team. Your name appeared on a victims list recovered during the April
2026 takedown of a romance-and-investment scam ring operating out of West
Africa (court documents will be made available to you under seal once your
identity is verified).

I am pleased to inform you that **$18,420.00 USD** in cryptocurrency, traced
to a wallet associated with your case, has been frozen in a court-supervised
escrow and approved for repatriation to verified victims under the United
States Marshals Service victim-restitution program.

Your refund is currently allocated to you under case ID BARC-2026-0518. To
release the funds we will need three items:

  1. A small "gas fee" payment of $480.00 in BTC or USDC. This is a
     non-negotiable network charge - the court does not accept ACH for
     blockchain repatriation.

  2. A copy of your photo ID (driver license or passport) and a recent
     utility bill as proof of address.

  3. The wallet address you would like the refund deposited to. If you do
     not currently hold a crypto wallet, our office can create one for you
     at no charge during the verification call.

You will receive your full $18,420 within 48 hours of confirmation. The
recovery window for this batch closes on Wednesday, May 13, 2026 - any funds
not claimed by that deadline will be forfeited back to the US Marshals
Service general victim-restitution pool and cannot be reissued.

Please review your case and respond using our secure case portal:

  https://blockchain-asset-recovery-coalition.org/case/BARC-2026-0518/claim

I am personally handling your file and am available through the portal at
any time. Our coalition has already returned over $46 million to families
this year and I am looking forward to closing your case for you.

